From da47d149009029e0ac6387535b9aaf9302bbf154 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: s1oplus <victorgarcez@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] grate: textures, blending and wlroots' GLES2 shaders

grate's TGSI fragment compiler only handles MOV, there were no sampler
views and the blend state was ignored, so wlroots' GLES2 renderer
crashed on its first textured draw.

Tegra20 blends in the fragment program, so instead of a general
compiler, recognise the fragment shaders wlroots uses (solid colour,
texture * alpha, RGBX texture * alpha; Mesa's clear quad is the solid
one) and run hand-written programs (fp/wlr/*.asm, assembled with
xf86-video-opentegra's assembler into fp/wlr/wlr_programs.h). Each comes
without blending and as premultiplied "over" (ONE, ONE_MINUS_SRC_ALPHA),
chosen at draw time from the blend state.

Also adds sampler views and sampler states for the fragment stage,
texture descriptors (format, filters, wrap, NPOT sizes), fragment
uniforms in fx10, and limits sampled formats to ones the 3D unit reads.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
