diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/grate/fp/wlr/README b/src/gallium/drivers/grate/fp/wlr/README
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0b03553
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/grate/fp/wlr/README
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+Hand-written Tegra20 fragment programs for the fixed shaders of wlroots'
+GLES2 renderer (solid quad, textured quad), in grate/opentegra assembler
+syntax. grate's TGSI fragment compiler only handles MOV, so
+grate_create_fs_state() recognises these TGSI shapes and uses the programs
+below instead. Tegra20 blends in the fragment program, so each comes in a
+"blending off" and a premultiplied "over" (ONE, ONE_MINUS_SRC_ALPHA) form.
+
+Uniforms (fx10 halves, 1.0 = 256):
+  u0.l u0.h u1.l u1.h  solid: colour in render-target byte order
+                       tex:   alpha, alpha, alpha, alpha
+  u2.l                 tex: 1.0 = ignore texture alpha (RGBX)
+  u2.h                 tex: 1.0 = swap bytes 0 and 2 (RGBA texture,
+                       BGRA target or the other way round)
+
+Rebuild wlr_programs.h with NuraXoom's packages/mesa-grate/gen-wlr-fp.sh.
